WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.079 --> 00:00:04.890
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here,
and today I'm breaking down the first full

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:08.940
official Avengers: Infinity War trailer for
easter eggs and other interesting details

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:10.280
you might have missed.

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:14.150
If you're new to my channel, I do regular
comic-book movie videos, and to celebrate

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:18.340
the Infinity War trailer finally dropping,
I'm kicking off a new superhero giveaway for

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:19.710
all my subscribers.

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:24.019
I've got full details on that plus the winners
of my Justice League giveaway later in this

00:00:24.019 --> 00:00:25.019
video.

00:00:25.019 --> 00:00:28.360
I'm gonna kick off with Bruce Banner because,
not only does his first shot in the trailer

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:33.300
give us a very cool easter egg, but also because
since Mark Ruffalo joined the MCU in the first

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:38.610
Avengers movie, he's given us the awesome
big-screen Banner and Hulk I've always wanted.

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:42.430
In the Infinity War trailer, we see Bruce
Banner back on Earth where it looks like he's

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:46.650
crashed through the ceiling of Doctor Strange's
Sanctum Sanctorum as the Hulk and smashed

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:47.720
through the floor.

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:51.510
It reminds me of Banner's crash-landing in
the Avengers movie when he met Harry Dean

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:53.370
Stanton's security guard.

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:57.830
This scene is a very cool nod to the first
issue of the Infinity Gauntlet comics in which

00:00:57.830 --> 00:01:02.390
Silver Surfer crashes through the roof of
Doctor Strange's Sanctum Sanctorum to warn

00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:04.710
of Thanos's impending arrival.

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:09.120
This is very likely also Banner arriving back
on Earth to warn the Avengers about Thanos

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:13.050
because, if you recall at the end of Thor:
Ragnarok, Hulk was with Thor when Thanos's

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:16.720
Sanctuary ship arrived to intercept the God
of Thunder's ship.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:20.180
Also notice in this shot that Tony Stark is
holding a little phone and it looks like it

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:24.720
could be the same one that Cap had FedExed
to him at the end of Civil War.

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:29.520
Talking of Bruce Banner, we have an intriguing
shot later in the trailer of him in Wakanda

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:31.940
standing next to a huge Hulkbuster arm.

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:35.700
Later again we see the Hulkbuster, which looks
different than last time we saw it, and it's

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:40.370
in action in Wakanda; and it feels like there's
a hint here that we may see Bruce Banner getting

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:43.620
into the Hulkbuster for Infinity War rather
than Tony Stark.

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:47.860
There are other possibilities too, though,
and I wonder if it could be T'Challa's sister

00:01:47.860 --> 00:01:49.170
Shuri in the suit?

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:52.933
We already know that Shuri is an engineering
and robotics expert with skills that are on

00:01:52.933 --> 00:01:54.450
a par with Tony Stark.

00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:59.460
Also, in that huge Wakandan battle, Hulk is
already there without any suit and I can't

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:01.000
see Shuri in that line-up.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:05.130
And, on top of that, we've already seen an
important Wakandan character suit up in Black

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:07.510
Panther-style Hulkbuster armour in the comics.

00:02:07.510 --> 00:02:12.490
Also, look a bit more closely at this amazing
line-up because Cap has some interesting arm

00:02:12.490 --> 00:02:13.490
shields.

00:02:13.490 --> 00:02:16.810
I think those could be some cool Wakandan
tech that's been designed for him.

00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:21.910
And, of course, after Cap abandoned his shield
at the end of Civil War, I just loved Black

00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:26.320
Panther's line, "get this man a shield", so
I wonder if that smart Wakandan tech could

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:31.350
make a shield materialise in a similar way
to how Black Panther's suit appears here.

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:36.610
Also, notice how Captain America no longer
has his star on his costume, which is understandable

00:02:36.610 --> 00:02:40.440
given that, after the events of Civil War,
he's now a fugitive on the run.

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:45.440
That, plus Steve Roger's beard, symbolise
his changed role in the MCU and are a nod

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:49.751
to the comics where he took on a new identity
as Nomad when he took off his Captain America

00:02:49.751 --> 00:02:54.069
costume after becoming disillusioned due to
the corruption of the US government.

00:02:54.069 --> 00:02:58.510
As for his beard, that seems like a hat-tip
to Captain America's Castaway in Dimension

00:02:58.510 --> 00:02:59.819
Z storyline in the comics.

00:02:59.819 --> 00:03:04.790
There's also a very quick shot in the trailer
of Steve Rogers catching a spear from one

00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:06.260
of Thanos's Black Order.

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:11.620
That figure, which we only get a glimpse of
here, is Proxima Midnight, who in the comics

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:14.530
was sent by Thanos to retrieve an infinity
gem.

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:19.130
And in the trailer, it looks like we see Proxima,
plus one of her Black Order comrades, Corvus

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:21.090
Glaive, attacking Vision's Mind Stone.

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:25.210
Like Cap, Black Widow is also sporting a new
look in Infinity War.

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:29.810
Her change from red hair to blonde is likely
because, like Cap, she's had to go underground

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:31.890
to lie low from the authorities.

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:35.830
When we last saw Natasha in Civil War, she
switched sides from Team Iron Man to help

00:03:35.830 --> 00:03:40.379
Cap escape at Berlin airport, and Tony Stark
later warned her that the government would

00:03:40.379 --> 00:03:41.690
be coming for her.

00:03:41.690 --> 00:03:46.739
Now, I think we can all agree the Battle in
Wakanda looks pretty epic and is a huge hint

00:03:46.739 --> 00:03:50.120
that Thanos is after something there, most
probably the Soul Stone.

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:54.390
And, if you're wondering what those four-armed
creatures are, well, they're Outriders.

00:03:54.390 --> 00:03:59.140
In the comics, Outriders are genetically-engineered
beings used by Corvus Glaive and Thanos to

00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:01.989
scout out worlds for tributes for the Mad
Titan.

00:04:01.989 --> 00:04:06.940
The Outriders lack their own free will and
are essentially cannon fodder for their masters.

00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:11.599
The trailer also reveals a battle in New York
with a huge portal-like ship or generator

00:04:11.599 --> 00:04:12.950
appearing over New York.

00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:17.479
And this is where we get an awesome shot of
Spider-Man, who's now wearing the Iron Spider

00:04:17.479 --> 00:04:20.680
suit he turned down at the end of Spider-Man:
Homecoming.

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:25.150
Spidey seems to fail at stopping whatever
is going on here and gets a beating from Thanos,

00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:29.189
but I wonder whether the next shot of Thor
in another huge circular object could be the

00:04:29.189 --> 00:04:32.659
God of Thunder inside the heart of whatever
is driving this generator?

00:04:32.659 --> 00:04:36.210
OK, let's look at Vision and Scarlet Witch
now.

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:40.029
We know already that Vision gets attacked
for his Mind Stone, but earlier we get to

00:04:40.029 --> 00:04:44.370
see him together with Wanda and what's curious
is that we're seeing him for the first time

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:48.360
with a human face, although it looks like
he's still got the yellow Mind Stone in his

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:49.360
forehead.

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:52.939
I wonder if he has the ability to switch between
android and human form?

00:04:52.939 --> 00:04:56.979
Also notice that Vision appears to be sharing
a room with Wanda, a big hint that we're seeing

00:04:56.979 --> 00:05:01.349
their relationship progress from just cooking
Paprikash together to something a lot more

00:05:01.349 --> 00:05:05.400
serious, another nod to how the couple also
got together in the comics.

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:10.279
By the way, a small thing I noticed is that
we never actually see Corvus Glaive extract

00:05:10.279 --> 00:05:14.689
the Mind Stone from Vision, so I wonder whether
there's a chance the Black Order here could

00:05:14.689 --> 00:05:19.330
be manipulating the Stone leaving it in Vision
and placing him under their control.

00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:23.809
So, what about the other two stones we see
in Thanos's infinity gauntlet in the trailer?

00:05:23.809 --> 00:05:28.570
Well, the blue stone will be the Space Stone
which we see Loki offering up to Thanos.

00:05:28.570 --> 00:05:32.309
This scene very likely happens on board the
ship that Loki and Thor are on at the end

00:05:32.309 --> 00:05:36.210
of Thor: Ragnarok and is strong confirmation
that Loki stole the Tesseract from Odin's

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:38.900
treasure room on Asgard at the end of that
movie.

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:43.699
You can see the carnage that Thanos has inflicted
on board the ship because these body markings

00:05:43.699 --> 00:05:46.930
match those from Asgardians in the last Thor
film.

00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:50.759
Although Loki is probably trying to save his
own skin here, I wonder whether there's a

00:05:50.759 --> 00:05:54.650
chance he's offering up the stone to save
the remaining Asgardians as well?

00:05:54.650 --> 00:05:59.629
And the purple stone that Thanos already has
will be the Power Stone which was given to

00:05:59.629 --> 00:06:01.809
the Nova Corps for safekeeping by the Guardians
of the Galaxy.

00:06:01.809 --> 00:06:06.599
There's a shot in the trailer of Thor looking
out over a planet which seems to be burning.

00:06:06.599 --> 00:06:11.210
I think it could actually be Xandar, home
of the Nova Corps and therefore show the aftermath

00:06:11.210 --> 00:06:12.659
of Thanos's attack.

00:06:12.659 --> 00:06:16.909
So, in the trailer we have an idea of how
Thanos has got hold of three of the six Infinity

00:06:16.909 --> 00:06:21.599
Stones he's after, but there's obviously three
more he has to get: the Reality Stone, the

00:06:21.599 --> 00:06:25.909
Soul Stone and the Time Stone, and I may do
a video with details on where we can expect

00:06:25.909 --> 00:06:26.909
to see those.

00:06:26.909 --> 00:06:31.110
By the way, another cool detail you might
have missed is that the words spoken by Nick

00:06:31.110 --> 00:06:35.149
Fury and the other Avengers at the start of
the trailer were actually originally spoken

00:06:35.149 --> 00:06:37.509
by Nick Fury in the first Avengers movie.

00:06:37.509 --> 00:06:41.559
"There was an idea, Stark knows this..."

00:06:41.559 --> 00:06:48.279
"The idea was to bring together a group of
remarkable people to see if they could become

00:06:48.279 --> 00:06:50.089
something more.

00:06:50.089 --> 00:06:57.229
To see if they could work together when we
needed them to, to fight the battles that

00:06:57.229 --> 00:06:59.319
we never could."

00:06:59.319 --> 00:07:02.110
"There was an idea..."

00:07:02.110 --> 00:07:06.259
"To bring together a group of remarkable people..."

00:07:06.259 --> 00:07:11.650
"To see if we could become something more..."

00:07:11.650 --> 00:07:16.349
"So when they needed us..."

00:07:16.349 --> 00:07:19.330
"We could fight the battles..."

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:23.039
"That they never could."

00:07:23.039 --> 00:07:27.089
And Marvel also sneakily includes those words
in their written form in the current Marvel

00:07:27.089 --> 00:07:28.409
Studios intro.

00:07:28.409 --> 00:07:31.800
So, did the Infinity War trailer live up to
your expectations?

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:35.460
And were there any other cool easter eggs
or details you spotted?

